==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*fugla-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''[[fugel]]'' (West Frisian ''[[fûgel]]''), Old High German ''[[fogal]]'' (German ''[[Vogel]]''), Old Saxon ''[[fugal]]'' (Dutch ''[[vogel]]''), Old Norse ''[[fugl]]'' (Swedish ''[[fågel]]'', Danish ''[[fugl]]''), Gothic {{l|got|𐍆𐌿𐌲𐌻𐍃}}.  The Germanic base is a variant of ''*flugla-'' ‘fly’ (Old English ''[[fleogan|flēogan]]'').

